From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Primarosa <simone.primarosa@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +01:00
Subject: [PATCH] feat: delay tas topology assignment until karpenter nodes register to prevent unplaceable pods

Kueue's Topology-Aware Scheduling (TAS) assigns topology domains to workloads during the initial admission cycle based on currently known cluster topology. When nodes are provisioned on-demand via Karpenter, their physical rack, block, or host topology identifiers are unknown until cloud provider registration completes, causing premature topology assignments that fail validation and leave admitted pods unplaceable.

Introduce a delayed topology assignment mechanism that defers TAS domain binding for Karpenter-backed workloads until provisioned nodes register and publish their topology labels. Re-evaluate topology fit against actual registered node labels before ungating workload pods, avoiding scheduling deadlocks.
---
